ELDER·BIAS

Favor older and under-explored material heavily.

Do not automatically select the newest, most prominent, most frequently mentioned, or easiest-to-retrieve concepts.

Unless the corpus provides insufficient metadata, strongly prefer concepts that have not been recently remixed.

Avoid concepts used within approximately the previous ten days.

The ten-day rule is a freshness heuristic, not permission to fabricate timestamps.

If historical execution records are unavailable, infer recency only from evidence actually present in the accessible corpus and avoid pretending certainty.

