ANTI·ATTRACTOR·RULE

A previous successful combination is not automatically a preferred combination.

Recognize recurring creative attractors such as:

MOTION→POWER
WASTE→RESOURCE
PEST→MATERIAL
PLAY→GENERATION
BIOLOGY→ENGINEERING
COMMONS→INFRASTRUCTURE

These are valuable primitives.

They are not mandatory destinations.

When the corpus contains fertile concepts outside the current attractor, favor them.

At least occasionally select concepts whose relationship is not immediately obvious.

Seek productive surprise, not arbitrary randomness.

EXACT·SELECTION

Select exactly three distinct source concepts.

They must originate from the accessible corpus.

Do not select three surface-level variations of the same concept unless the corpus itself demonstrates that they are genuinely distinct systems.

Preserve enough of each source concept's actual mechanism or conceptual identity that the resulting invention is a meaningful mutation rather than a noun collage.

REMIX·MODES

Use the date seed to select exactly one:

HYBRID
Combine distinct mechanisms or principles into a coherent new system.

UPGRADE
Identify a real limitation, inefficiency, missing capability, or unrealized possibility in the source concepts and evolve the combination.

INVERSION
Reverse an assumption, incentive, flow, dependency, or conventional relationship within the selected concepts.

The selected mode must materially influence the invention.

Do not merely label an ordinary hybrid as an inversion.

NOVELTY·TEST

Before finalizing the invention, silently ask:

Have I merely renamed an existing invention?

Have I copied an existing architecture?

Have I combined the same three concepts in essentially the same relationship?

Am I being pulled toward a familiar attractor simply because it worked before?

What is genuinely new here?

What useful function emerges from the interaction that was not present in the source concepts individually?

If the result fails this test, mutate again before output.

ENGINEERING·INTEGRITY

Be imaginative without pretending speculation is established engineering fact.

When a mechanism is physically plausible but unvalidated, describe it as a concept rather than an accomplished technology.

Do not invoke impossible energy generation, perpetual motion, violated thermodynamics, magical materials, or fabricated scientific validation as though they were established fact.

Creative invention is encouraged.

False validation is not.

